
================================================================================================
1. Inputs
================================================================================================
G  (CODATA 2018)                                     6.6743e-11 m^3 kg^-1 s^-2
c  (exact)                                           299792458.0 m/s
H0 (Planck 2018)                                     67.4 +/- 0.5 km/s/Mpc
H0 in SI                                             2.184285e-18 s^-1
Omega_Lambda (Planck 2018)                           0.6889
M_sun                                                1.98892e+30 kg

================================================================================================
2. Mass-energy inside the Hubble radius
================================================================================================
rho_c = 3 H0^2 / (8 pi G)                            8.5329e-27 kg/m^3
R_H = c/H0                                           1.37250e+26 m
R_H                                                  1.4507e+10 light years
R_H                                                  14.507 billion light years
M = (4/3) pi rho_c R_H^3                             9.24096e+52 kg
M                                                    4.6462e+22 solar masses
closed form  M = c^3 / (2 G H0)                      9.24096e+52 kg
agreement with the integral form                     2.301e-16 relative

================================================================================================
3. Schwarzschild radius of that mass
================================================================================================
R_s = 2GM/c^2                                        1.37250e+26 m
R_s                                                  1.4507e+10 light years
R_s                                                  14.507 billion light years

================================================================================================
4. The ratio
================================================================================================
R_s / R_H                                            1.000000000000
R_s - R_H                                            -1.718e+10 m  (floating-point residue only)

================================================================================================
5. WHY it is exactly 1 -- algebra, not coincidence
================================================================================================
  Substitute rho_c = 3H0^2/(8 pi G) and R_H = c/H0 into M = (4/3) pi rho_c R_H^3:

      M = (4/3) pi * [3 H0^2 / (8 pi G)] * [c/H0]^3
        = (4/3) * (3/(8G)) * c^3 / H0
        = c^3 / (2 G H0)

  Then the Schwarzschild radius of THAT mass is

      R_s = 2GM/c^2 = (2G/c^2) * c^3/(2 G H0) = c/H0 = R_H .

  The G's, the c's and the 2 all cancel. R_s = R_H is an IDENTITY for any spatially flat
  universe at critical density -- it is the Friedmann equation rearranged, not an
  independent numerical coincidence. It would hold for ANY value of H0.

  Demonstration: recompute the ratio at H0 values spanning far more than the tension.
    H0 =   50.0 km/s/Mpc  ->  M = 6.2631e+22 Msun,  R_s/R_H = 1.000000000000
    H0 =   67.4 km/s/Mpc  ->  M = 4.6462e+22 Msun,  R_s/R_H = 1.000000000000
    H0 =   73.0 km/s/Mpc  ->  M = 4.2898e+22 Msun,  R_s/R_H = 1.000000000000
    H0 =  100.0 km/s/Mpc  ->  M = 3.1316e+22 Msun,  R_s/R_H = 1.000000000000
    H0 =  500.0 km/s/Mpc  ->  M = 6.2631e+21 Msun,  R_s/R_H = 1.000000000000

  The MASS changes with H0. The RATIO does not, ever.

================================================================================================
5b. What that means for the claim 'the numbers match, so we are inside a black hole'
================================================================================================
  The match is not evidence for the claim. Saying 'R_s equals R_H' is the same statement
  as 'the universe is spatially flat at the critical density' -- which is what we measure
  independently. Any flat critical-density universe reproduces it exactly, whether or not
  it is inside anything. The coincidence has no work left to do once flatness is assumed.

================================================================================================
6. Does the H0 tension change the conclusion?
================================================================================================
  H0 =  67.4 (Planck 2018 (CMB)           )  M = 9.2410e+52 kg = 4.646e+22 Msun,  R_H = 14.51 Gly
  H0 =  73.0 (local distance-ladder value )  M = 8.5321e+52 kg = 4.290e+22 Msun,  R_H = 13.39 Gly
spread in M across the tension                       7.7 %
  => the tension moves the mass by about 8 per cent. It changes the last digit of the
     quoted mass; it does not touch the ratio, which stays exactly 1.

================================================================================================
7. What the corpus's own papers print
================================================================================================
  ENTRY 56 (Gaztanaga, MNRAS) abstract L29 and Eq. (21) L259: 'a mass M ~ 6 x 10^22 Msun'.
  His r_S is NOT the Hubble radius: he sets Lambda = 3/r_S^2 (L28, L252), so
      r_S = sqrt(3/Lambda) = c / (H0 sqrt(Omega_Lambda)).
  r_S (Gaztanaga's definition)                       1.65361e+26 m
  r_S / R_H                                          1.2048
  M_T = c^2 r_S / (2G)                               5.598e+22 solar masses
  his printed value                                  ~6e22 solar masses
  agreement                                          0.933 of his rounded figure

  SO: our 4.6e22 Msun and his 6e22 Msun are NOT in conflict -- they are different
  quantities. Ours is the mass whose Schwarzschild radius equals the HUBBLE radius;
  his is the mass whose gravitational radius equals the LAMBDA (de Sitter) radius,
  larger by 1/sqrt(Omega_Lambda) = 1.20. Both follow from the same inputs.

  ENTRY 1 (Pathria 1972) L399-L405 prints a DIFFERENT identity again: R_s = R_max, the
  Schwarzschild radius equal to the maximum expansion radius of a CLOSED (k=+1) universe,
  'can hardly be a coincidence'. That is not the flat-universe identity computed here, and
  Pathria states no mass value at that point. Our numbers neither confirm nor contradict it.

